  "taskCall": {
    "context": "# Goal\nKengaku lane, round 68: ONE v1 wave of 12 seats (build + attack). You are ONE seat of this wave. The round's two claims are FROZEN in /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin/plans/round-68-claims.md (read it first, in full). Predicates, counters, kill rules, the frozen case table and the controls are fixed there. No seat changes them. A seat that thinks a rule is wrong reports it in its output and does not edit it.\n\n# State you read (working tree; uncommitted round-68 bytes are real)\n- The receipt of record `corpus/evidence/round68/pypi/receipt.txt` and its evidence (per-case stderr captures under `corpus/evidence/round68/pypi/stderr/`, `corpus/evidence/round68/pypi/server-log.txt`) exist in the working tree, produced by the L1's scored battery run AFTER the freeze. They are not yet committed; that is expected — the L1 lands them after this wave.\n- The instruments `plans/round68_c1_pypi_finish.py` and `plans/round68_c2_correction_gate.py` are committed at the freeze; their bytes are the frozen instruments.\n\n# Paths (absolute; every `Report:` trailer path is relative to /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin — write it at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin/<that path>)\n- L = /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin (lane repo). Write NOTHING in L except where your item below names a path; read-only seats write only their own subdir under L/.ufo/waves/round-68/w1/ and their scratch.\n- W = L/.ufo/waves/round-68/w1 (wave dir; your report file goes here, named <YourSeatName>.md)\n- S = /fast/scratch/hyaku/kengaku-r68/<YourSeatName> (your scratch root; create it with mkdir -p; delete it before you yield — `trap 'rm -rf -- \"$S\"' EXIT` in shell, `finally: shutil.rmtree` in Python; receipts you must keep go into W first)\n\n# Bounds (binding)\n- No git or jj command that mutates anything (no add/commit/push/stash/checkout/reset/rebase); no edits outside L; no edits to plans/round-68-claims.md, SKILL.md, corpus/SOURCES.md, SCORECARD.md, LOG.md, PROVINCE.md — the L1 integrates those from your drafts.\n- Port 8080 is owned by the L1's battery run: NEVER start or bind anything on 127.0.0.1:8080 (round-63 lesson: concurrent seats contended for the port and confounded the cases).\n- /tmp is for files under 50 MB only; never hardcode /tmp in anything that gets committed.\n- pacman is PAUSED host-wide (operator guard): install nothing via pacman; uv tool / npx / an official binary in ~/.local/bin only, and record any install (tool, version, channel, reason) in your report.\n- Tooling authorization (operator, 2026-10-19): you may install or upgrade tools that help your item — read /home/vgpnk/.omp/agent/RULES.md first (official channels, update-safety gate, record tool/version/channel/reason).\n- You are one seat of a swarm: no delegation, no background jobs, no subagent spawns.\n- Honesty: an unrun check has not passed; report defects and mismatches exactly as found, never papered over.\n\n# Output\nWrite your findings to W/<YourSeatName>.md and end your final message with a 5-line summary: verdict, evidence paths, anything the L1 must integrate.",
    "tasks": [
      {
        "name": "PypiReplicate",
        "agent": "executor",
        "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nReplication run of the frozen R68-C1 battery (the round-65 replication precedent). The scored receipt of record is L/corpus/evidence/round68/pypi/receipt.txt; your run must NOT overwrite it or any file under L/corpus/evidence/round68/pypi/.\n1. Read plans/round-68-claims.md (R68-C1 section) and plans/round68_c1_pypi_finish.py (run_battery, check_receipt, the --evidence-dir flag).\n2. Run a SECOND fresh battery entirely inside your scratch: `python3 plans/round68_c1_pypi_finish.py --lane /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin --work S/replicate --receipt S/replicate/receipt-replicate.txt --evidence-dir S/replicate/evidence` with the exit captured in-runner (`rc=$?` echoed into your receipt copy). The battery binds port 8080 — run it exactly once, and if it reports SETUP port-8080-occupied, report that and stop (do not retry).\n3. Compare the replication receipt against the receipt of record: the PREDICTION-VECTOR and the four CASE observed/expected fields must be identical; the per-case stderr_sha256 values must be identical (byte-stable captures — if any differs, show the exact differing bytes with `diff` of the two capture files and report it as a finding, not a failure you fix); index_pid values are expected to differ (ephemeral pids, not a defect).\n4. Write W/PypiReplicate.md: the in-runner rc, the comparison table, and a verdict line `REPLICATION vector=<match|diff> stderr-shas=<match|diff>`.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch except your single labrat.\nJudged on: coverage, calibration\nMilestone: kengaku r68 w1 (v1, 12 seats: build + attack): R68-C1 pypi-server corrected stderr re-freeze (coverage, L0-capped); R68-C2 round-67 routed defects as dated corrections (calibration); frontier drafts and source open\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-68/w1/PypiReplicate.md"
      },
      {
        "name": "GateRedRun",
        "agent": "executor",
        "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nRe-run and pin the R68-C2 correction gate's red state (the corrections are NOT landed yet — the L1 lands them after this wave; your run must stay red).\n1. Read plans/round-68-claims.md (R68-C2 section) and plans/round68_c2_correction_gate.py in full.\n2. Run `python3 plans/round68_c2_correction_gate.py` with the exit captured in-runner; write the output to W/gate/red-before-recheck.txt. It must print `DEFECTS n=5` and `PREDICATE R68-C2 fail` with rc 1 — the same five defects as the freeze-time receipt L/.ufo/waves/round-68/w1/gate/red-before.txt (compare the two files; report any difference in the defect list as a finding).\n3. Run `python3 plans/round68_c2_correction_gate.py --selftest --work S/gate` with the exit captured in-runner; write the output to W/gate/selftest-recheck.txt. It must print `SELFTEST defects-in-fake=5 want=5 all-fail=True` with rc 0.\n4. Verify each check E1–E5 implements its frozen clause sentence-by-sentence (the claims doc's R68-C2 check list); report any check whose code does not match its frozen sentence.\n5. Write W/GateRedRun.md: both rc captures, the comparison, the clause-by-clause verdict, and a line `GATE red-reproduced=<True|False> selftest=<ok|broken>`.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch except your single labrat.\nJudged on: coverage, calibration\nMilestone: kengaku r68 w1 (v1, 12 seats: build + attack): R68-C1 pypi-server corrected stderr re-freeze (coverage, L0-capped); R68-C2 round-67 routed defects as dated corrections (calibration); frontier drafts and source open\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-68/w1/GateRedRun.md"
      },
