        "agent": "executor",
        "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nProduce the committed round-67 probe self-test tally (routed defect 3 of the round-67 closure: the tally was quoted but never committed).\n1. Read plans/round-68-claims.md (R68-C2, check E3) and skim plans/round67_c1_pipeline_probe.py (its --selftest mode only; do not modify it).\n2. Run `python3 plans/round67_c1_pipeline_probe.py --selftest --work S/tally` with the exit captured in-runner (`rc=$?`). Expected: `SELFTEST green_rc=0 red_rc=1 ok` with rc 0 — but record whatever it actually prints.\n3. Write the tally to L/corpus/evidence/round68/r67-probe-selftest.txt (this is the one file your item writes into L) with exactly this shape: line 1 `# R67 probe --selftest tally (round 68: routed defect 3, committed evidence)`; line 2 `# date: <UTC ISO>`; line 3 `PROBE sha256=<sha256 of plans/round67_c1_pipeline_probe.py, computed by you>`; line 4 the command; then the verbatim captured output; last line `rc=<captured exit>`.\n4. Also run `python3 plans/round67_c1_pipeline_probe.py --check-receipt corpus/evidence/round67/pipe/receipt.txt` (in-runner exit capture) and record its last line — expected `PREDICATE R67-C1 pass` rc 0.\n5. Write W/SelftestTally.md: the tally file path, the captured rc values, and a line `TALLY committed=<path> selftest-ok=<True|False> check-receipt=<pass|fail>`.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch except your single labrat.\nJudged on: coverage, calibration\nMilestone: kengaku r68 w1 (v1, 12 seats: build + attack): R68-C1 pypi-server corrected stderr re-freeze (coverage, L0-capped); R68-C2 round-67 routed defects as dated corrections (calibration); frontier drafts and source open\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-68/w1/SelftestTally.md"
