        "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nFalsify the round's two claims (read-only on L; fixtures in scratch; write W/ClaimFalsify.md).\n1. Read plans/round-68-claims.md in full — the predicates, kill rules and controls are the target; a rule you think is wrong is reported, never edited.\n2. Attack R68-C1's counter with forged receipts (build them in S/forge/, run `python3 plans/round68_c1_pypi_finish.py --check-receipt <forged>` on each, capture rc): (f1) the round-63 amended receipt L/corpus/evidence/round63/pypi-probe.txt scored against the NEW counter — must be refused (it lacks every new binding); (f2) a copy of the receipt of record with one CASE observed flipped P→F or F→P — must be refused; (f3) a copy with the K2 stderr_sha256 replaced by the sha of any other case's capture — must be refused; (f4) a copy with the server-log sha replaced by the stderr sha — must be refused; (f5) a copy with `CLASS network-service executed=2` edited to executed=1 — must be refused. For each: the exact defect line the checker printed.\n3. Attack the kill rules: state for each of (a)–(e) whether the frozen text gives a seat or the L1 room to narrow the predicate after data; the round-63 A1 lesson (a detector widened after the miss) is the class to check for.\n4. Attack R68-C2: is the correction gate's red-before a genuine before-state (the corrections really absent), or could the gate pass pre-landing? Try `python3 plans/round68_c2_correction_gate.py` yourself and check the five defect reasons are the ABSENCE reasons, not crashes.\n5. Write W/ClaimFalsify.md with a line per attack: `FALSIFY <id> refused=<True|False> defect=<line>` and a final verdict naming any surviving forgery or rule gap.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: coverage, calibration\nMilestone: kengaku r68 w1 (v1, 12 seats: build + attack): R68-C1 pypi-server corrected stderr re-freeze (coverage, L0-capped); R68-C2 round-67 routed defects as dated corrections (calibration); frontier drafts and source open\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-68/w1/ClaimFalsify.md"
      },
