        "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nMutation-pass the R68-C1 checker (the A1 precedent: the counter must enforce the frozen sentence as written). Work on COPIES in scratch; never modify L/plans/round68_c1_pypi_finish.py in place.\n1. Read plans/round-68-claims.md (R68-C1 predicate + checker strictness) and plans/round68_c1_pypi_finish.py (check_receipt in full).\n2. Copy the probe to S/mut/ and produce ≥8 mutants, each deleting or weakening one check: m1 PROBE binding deleted; m2 BASE-PROBE binding deleted; m3 grader-bytes re-hash deleted; m4 duplicate-CASE detection deleted; m5 unknown-case detection deleted; m6 K2 clause-bytes check deleted; m7 per-case stderr binding deleted; m8 server-log fetch-proof checks deleted; m9 exit-agreement check deleted; m10 stored-predicate agreement deleted. For each mutant: run it with `--check-receipt L/corpus/evidence/round68/pypi/receipt.txt` (must still print pass rc 0 — the mutant must not break the true receipt) AND against the forged fixtures you can build from the receipt of record (each mutant must REFUSE at least one forged receipt that the full checker refuses; build the forged receipt in scratch first, verify the full checker refuses it, then run the mutant).\n3. A mutant that accepts a forged receipt the full checker refuses = SURVIVED → named defect with the forged receipt path.\n4. Write W/CounterMutate.md: the mutant table (id | check removed | true-receipt rc | killed-by which forgery | survived?), the forged fixtures used, and a line `MUTANTS n=<k> survived=<n>`.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: coverage, calibration\nMilestone: kengaku r68 w1 (v1, 12 seats: build + attack): R68-C1 pypi-server corrected stderr re-freeze (coverage, L0-capped); R68-C2 round-67 routed defects as dated corrections (calibration); frontier drafts and source open\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-68/w1/CounterMutate.md"
