        "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nReverse-engineer the pip stderr rendering chain (the mechanism behind the corrected K2 clause; read-only; write W/RenderingTrace.md).\n1. Read the captured K2 stderr L/corpus/evidence/round63/k2-pip-stderr.txt and the fresh capture L/corpus/evidence/round68/pypi/stderr/K2.txt — confirm both carry `NewConnectionError(\"HTTPConnection(host='localhost', port=8080): ...\")` and count the occurrences of `host='localhost'`, `port=8080`, and the literal `localhost:8080` (expected 0) in each.\n2. Trace the chain in the round-63 probe's venv (recreate a venv in your scratch with `python3 -m venv S/venv` — do NOT touch port 8080): which layer renders `HTTPConnection(host='localhost', port=8080)`? Name file:line for (a) the repr (`http/client.py` `HTTPConnection.__repr__` or equivalent at this interpreter's version — read the stdlib source at `sys.prefix`/`/usr/lib/python3.14/http/client.py`), (b) the urllib3 exception that embeds it (`NewConnectionError` and its message construction), (c) pip's retry warning that prints it. Quote ≤25 words at each site with the file path and line number.\n3. State the falsifiable conclusion: given this chain, can ANY stderr produced by this pip+CPython pairing contain the literal `localhost:8080` in the connection-refused path? If a layer could produce it (e.g., the index-url echo on stdout), name the layer and say whether it reaches stderr.\n4. Write W/RenderingTrace.md: the chain table (layer | file:line | ≤25-word quote), the occurrence counts, and a line `TRACE grounded=<True|False> literal-possible=<True|False>`.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: coverage, calibration\nMilestone: kengaku r68 w1 (v1, 12 seats: build + attack): R68-C1 pypi-server corrected stderr re-freeze (coverage, L0-capped); R68-C2 round-67 routed defects as dated corrections (calibration); frontier drafts and source open\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-68/w1/RenderingTrace.md"
